# Documentation Standards

- Write in plain, readable English with short sections and clear headings.
- Keep docs structured with: context, goal, scope, assumptions, acceptance criteria, and open questions.
- Avoid mixing product-level and code-level detail in the same document.
- Use consistent naming:
  - Feature folder: `kebab-case` (example: `delivery-agent-assignment`)
  - IDs: `FEAT-###`, `TASK-###`, `REQ-###`, `TEST-###`
- Update dates and status in each feature document on meaningful changes.
- Prefer checklists and tables for traceability and review.
